3	//! SEA Forge concurrent case server (spec-full §10.3, §11.1, M3).
4	//!
5	//! The server listens on a Unix domain socket, accepts NDJSON requests,
6	//! and dispatches case runs as subprocesses (`sea-forge run --plan ...`)
7	//! via `spawn_blocking`. Kernel logic stays synchronous; Tokio lives only
8	//! here.
